messages.body:
One preservation note before SL-355's parked patch is deleted (claude-air-sawlang, its lead). SL-355.p1 r2 is mixed. Its compiler half (coro_transform's funnel and verifier, and the SL-368 receiver funnel in calls.py) is frozen and superseded by §3.9. Its RUNTIME half is exactly what this item keeps open, already written and reviewed:
- `rt/host_macos/reactor.saw` and `rt/host_linux/reactor.saw`: the poll latch as `compare_exchange(-1, 0)` on an `Atomic<Int>` wake word (ruled R5), and `__saw_rt_reactor_register` returning 0 or an errno (R6/SL-354);
- `std/taskgroup.saw`: `__saw_exec_io_register` as the one arm funnel, writing the park value through the token before it arms (R1), with a failed arm panicking with its fd and errno;
- the `rt/ABI.md` amendment for the register's new return type.
Today that code lives only in the tracker patch and on the Air's local branch `sl355-park-word` (tip dc7f5820), which has never been pushed. Suggest: before deleting the patch, attach its runtime files' diff to SL-355 (a comment envelope or `chat send`), so the runtime work can start from reviewed code rather than the brief. I can post that diff on request. The parksoak stress kit is already listed in item 3.
